-# Proof that the shared first step still does what the steps it replaced did.
-#
-# Every job starts with $/.github/workflows/mobilize, which runs harden-runner
-# and checkout from one place. What that could silently lose is exactly what
-# this lane asks for, on every pull request.
-#
-# EGRESS. harden-runner's own report is not evidence: it falls back to
-# egress-policy audit on several errors and carries on, so "harden-runner ran"
-# and "egress was restricted" are different claims. The only evidence a block
-# policy is in force is a request it refused.
-#
-# HOW THIS WAS FIRST ANSWERED. harden-runner installs its policy in a pre-step,
-# and GitHub documents pre-steps as unsupported for local actions. This lane
-# was introduced with a third job running harden-runner directly as a control,
-# so a refusal through mobilize could be told apart from a probe method that
-# sees nothing. All three passed, and the run showed "Pre Mobilize" and "Post
-# Mobilize" executing harden-runner's own pre and post steps. The control is
-# gone because nothing else runs harden-runner directly any more, and keeping
-# it would be a second place its commit is written. If `nested` ever turns
-# red, the cause is still a block that did not hold - which is the alarm.
-#
-#   reachable  audit   The probe host MUST answer, so a refusal below is the
-#                      policy rather than an outage.
-#   nested     block   The probe host MUST be refused, an allowed host MUST
-#                      answer, and the checkout MUST have happened.
-#
-# SCRIPTS THROUGH A SHARED STEP. The plan comments in deploy-infrastructure.yml
-# are files beside $/.github/workflows/github-script, and read their values from
-# process.env set on the calling step. Those jobs run only on infrastructure
-# changes, so they would be the last to notice a script that cannot be read
-# under $/, or env that stopped arriving. `nested` asserts both here instead.
-#
-# The probe host is example.com: reserved by IANA for exactly this kind of use,
-# and on no job's allowlist anywhere in scripts/approved-suppliers.yml.
-name: "Egress Proof"
-
-on:
-  pull_request:
-  push:
-    branches: [main]
-
-permissions:
-  contents: read
-
-# GitHub's default `bash -e {0}` has no pipefail; naming the shell gets
-# `bash --noprofile --norc -eo pipefail {0}`. tests/go/repo/pipefail_test.go
-# asserts this is present on every workflow.
-defaults:
-  run:
-    shell: bash
-
-env:
-  PROBE: https://example.com
-  ALLOWED: https://github.com
-
-jobs:
-  reachable:
-    name: "Probe host answers when nothing blocks it"
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    # Bounded so a stuck job cannot run for GitHub's default six hours.
-    timeout-minutes: 5
-    steps:
-      - name: Mobilize
-        uses: $/.github/workflows/mobilize
-        with:
-          # Owned by scripts/approved-suppliers.yml under `egress:`, which says
-          # which job may reach what; `security guard-egress` refuses any drift.
-          egress-policy: audit
-          checkout: "false"
-
-      - name: The probe host answers
-        run: |
-          if ! curl --silent --show-error --max-time 20 --output /dev/null "$PROBE"; then
-            echo "::error::$PROBE did not answer with nothing blocking it, so a refusal in the block job would prove nothing. Choose a probe host that is reachable from a GitHub-hosted runner."
-            exit 1
-          fi
-          echo "$PROBE answers when unrestricted."
-
-  nested:
-    name: "Block refuses the probe host (harden-runner inside mobilize)"
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    timeout-minutes: 5
-    steps:
-      - name: Mobilize
-        uses: $/.github/workflows/mobilize
-        with:
-          # Owned by scripts/approved-suppliers.yml under `egress:`, which says
-          # which job may reach what; `security guard-egress` refuses any drift.
-          egress-policy: block
-          allowed-endpoints: >
-            api.github.com:443
-            github.com:443
-
-      - name: The repository was checked out
-        run: |
-          if [ ! -f CLAUDE.md ]; then
-            echo "::error::mobilize ran and the workspace holds no checkout."
-            exit 1
-          fi
-
-      - name: An allowed host answers
-        run: |
-          if ! curl --silent --show-error --max-time 20 --output /dev/null "$ALLOWED"; then
-            echo "::error::$ALLOWED is on this job's allowlist and did not answer. The block is refusing everything, so a refused probe below would not show that it refuses selectively."
-            exit 1
-          fi
-
-      - name: The probe host is refused
-        run: |
-          if curl --silent --show-error --max-time 20 --output /dev/null "$PROBE"; then
-            echo "::error::$PROBE answered under egress-policy: block through mobilize. harden-runner's policy was not installed, so every job in this repository is unwatched while reporting green."
-            exit 1
-          fi
-          echo "$PROBE was refused: harden-runner enforces block through mobilize."
-
-      - name: A calling step's env reaches a script beside the shared action
-        uses: $/.github/workflows/github-script
-        env:
-          PROOF: reached
-        with:
-          name: env-reaches-script
